        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Troy University, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute\n- Places: Troy, New York\n- Buildings: Folsom Library\n- Concepts: Brutalist architecture\n\nFacts:\n- Troy University was established in Troy, New York, in 1858.\n- Troy University was a short-lived university.\n- Folsom Library is a research library of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute in Troy, New York.\n- Folsom Library was constructed on the site of the former Troy University.\n- Folsom Library is located on the five-acre campus of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute.\n- Folsom Library was constructed in the Brutalist architectural style.",
